# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project documentation — ALWAYS tracked.
#
# History: commit bdc3c0a added a blanket `*.docx` rule with three per-file
# `!` exceptions, so every other Word document was silently invisible to git.
# Commit ad4ad87 dropped `*.docx`, but the previously-hidden files were never
# staged. The explicit negations below keep documentation tracked even if a
# broad binary-extension rule is reintroduced later.
#
# NOTE: these negations cannot rescue files inside an excluded directory
# (node_modules/, .next/, venv/, .ipynb_checkpoints/ ...) — that is intended.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!*.md
!*.docx
!*.doc
!*.pdf
!*.txt
!*.rtf
!*.csv
!*.xlsx
!*.xls
!*.pptx
!*.odt
!docs/
!docs/**

# Re-assert junk exclusions that the broad `!docs/**` negation would otherwise
# resurrect (a negated directory is descended into again by git).
.ipynb_checkpoints/
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/
docs/**/__pycache__/
docs/**/*.pyc

